<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch09-the-fundamental-theorem-of-calculus">
  <title>The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus</title>
  <shorttitle>The Fundamental Theorem</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>For a continuous function <m>f</m>, the accumulation function <m>A(x)=\int_a^x f(t)\,dt</m> has derivative <m>A\prime(x)=f(x)</m>. Conversely, an antiderivative <m>F</m> evaluates a definite integral by <m>\int_a^b f=F(b)-F(a)</m>. This chapter proves these two parts of the Fundamental Theorem and develops antiderivatives and substitution.</p></introduction>

